---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { profile, labExperience } from '../data/profile';
---
<BaseLayout title="About | Doan Van Tai" description="Doan Van Tai’s research journey from building an SDN network digital twin to studying routing decision quality under imperfect information.">
  <div class="container page-header"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Home</a><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</p><h1>About Doan Van Tai</h1><p class="page-description">My background, research journey, and the work I want to pursue.</p></div>
  <div class="container page-body about-page-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>{profile.bio}</p>
      <p>My Vietnamese name is <strong>Đoàn Văn Tài</strong>. I’m based in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, and expect to complete my Bachelor of Engineering in Computer Networks and Communications in 2027.</p>

      <h2>My research journey</h2>
      <p>I came to network research through building and testing systems. In <a href="/work/network-digital-twin/">DT4N</a>, I connected an SDN testbed to a digital representation and followed control commands through to their effects on the network.</p>
      <p>That experience led me to ask how a controller chooses an action when its view of the network is incomplete. My ongoing <a href="/work/state-model-regret/">State-Model-Regret study</a> takes up that question through models and simulation. I explain the connection in <a href="/writing/from-digital-twins-to-routing-decisions/">this research note</a>.</p>

      <h2>Current lab experience</h2>
      <p>I joined <strong>UIT InSecLab</strong> in November 2026 as a <strong>{labExperience.role}</strong>, exploring AI for Security.</p>
      <p>{labExperience.description} My current learning also includes retrieval and reinforcement learning.</p>
      <p><a href={labExperience.href}>View my current role and experience →</a></p>

      <h2>What I’m working toward</h2>
      <p>I want to develop as a Research Engineer who can connect theoretical reasoning, simulation, experimental evidence, and working systems. My longer-term interests include graduate research in computer networks, Network Digital Twins, and AI / ML for networking.</p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>I keep model assumptions, configurations, and measurement scripts with the code. I compare results with a defined reference and document failed targets alongside successful runs.</p>
      <h2>Research interests</h2>
      <ul>{profile.interests.map(interest => <li>{interest}</li>)}</ul>
      <p><a href="/research/">Explore my research studies and current research question →</a></p>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p><strong>University of Information Technology, VNU-HCM</strong><br/>B.Eng. Computer Networks and Communications<br/>2023 to 2027 (expected) · GPA 3.52 / 4.00</p>
      <h2>Technical toolkit</h2>
      <div class="skills-grid">{profile.skills.map(skill=><div class="skill-group"><h3>{skill.title}</h3><p>{skill.items}</p></div>)}</div>
      <h2>Let’s connect</h2>
      <p>I’m open to conversations about graduate research, future research or R&D opportunities, and projects in networking or AI for Security.</p>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> · <a href={profile.github}>GitHub</a></p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/cv/">View my CV <Icon size={15}/></a>
    </article>
    <figure class="about-page-photo"><div class="photo-viewport"><img src="/images/tai-sunset.jpg" alt="Doan Van Tai at the seaside beneath a pink sunset" width="1368" height="1824"/></div><figcaption>At the seaside.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
